ELD Ubuntu/PPA packaging
========================

This is a native source package built from the LLVM 22-compatible ELD release
line. Ubuntu's llvm-22-dev package is used directly; LLVM is not bundled.

ELD 22 is published for Ubuntu 26.10 (stonking) only. Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute)
keeps ELD 21 from the ubuntu_packaging branch on top of native-llvm21.

The ubuntu_packaging_llvm22 branch must always contain exactly one commit on
top of native-llvm22. Keep packaging edits in that commit:

  git switch ubuntu_packaging_llvm22
  git add <changed-files>
  git commit --amend --no-edit
  git push --force-with-lease rustedsword ubuntu_packaging_llvm22

When native-llvm22 advances, rebase the single packaging commit onto it, then
amend and force-push with lease. publish.sh verifies the branch, ancestry,
commit count, and clean-tree invariant before a normal upload.

Launchpad versions are immutable. Before each new upload, add a changelog entry
with a unique version (increment +gxrN), then amend the existing packaging
commit. The changelog targets stonking with a ~26.10.N suffix.

Publishing runs in an Ubuntu 26.04 Podman container. On the signing host, use
./publish.sh --no-upload for a signed validation build and ./publish.sh to sign
and upload the stonking build to ppa:lightofmysoul/gxr. Without a private key,
use ./publish.sh --unsigned; unsigned artifacts cannot be uploaded.
